---
const features = [
  { title: 'Multiple accounts', text: 'Connect more than one account per provider and see them side by side.' },
  { title: 'Remaining or used', text: 'One setting flips every bar, percentage and tray line. Remaining is the default.' },
  { title: 'Pinned accounts', text: 'Pin accounts from a provider page and the dashboard shows those instead of the first two.' },
  { title: 'Provider order', text: 'Reorder providers or hide one from the dashboard without disconnecting it.' },
  { title: 'Reauthenticate in place', text: 'When a Codex, Claude Code or Grok login expires, the card keeps your last numbers and offers a Reauthenticate button.' },
  { title: 'Import local accounts', text: 'Pull in Codex, Antigravity, Kiro, Cursor and Grok accounts you already signed into.' },
  { title: 'Dark and light', text: 'System, dark or light theme. Dark uses the lime accent, light switches to amber.' },
  { title: 'Safe export', text: 'Export account summaries as JSON. Tokens and API keys never go in the file.' },
];
---

<section class="features" aria-labelledby="features-title">
  <div class="q-wrap features__grid">
    <div class="features__intro">
      <h2 id="features-title">The small stuff that adds up</h2>
      <p>What the desktop app does besides the dashboard.</p>
    </div>
    <dl>
      {
        features.map((feature) => (
          <div>
            <dt>{feature.title}</dt>
            <dd>{feature.text}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>
  </div>

  <div class="q-wrap">
    <div class="privacy">
      <h2>Stays on your machine</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>No Quota server, no account to make, and no analytics.</li>
        <li>The desktop app keeps credentials in Rust-owned storage under <code>~/.quota</code>. The interface only sees safe summaries.</li>
        <li>quota-cli reads your agent CLIs' credentials and never writes to them.</li>
      </ul>
      <a href="/docs/privacy/">How storage works</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .features {
    padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 6rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--q-line-soft);
  }

  .features__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 60rem) {
    .features__grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 2.2fr);
      gap: 3.5rem;
    }
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 3.6vw, 2.5rem);
    max-width: 14ch;
  }

  .features__intro p {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--q-muted);
  }

  dl {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
    margin: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--q-line);
    border-left: 1px solid var(--q-line);
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    dl {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 80rem) {
    dl {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  dl > div {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--q-line);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--q-line);
  }

  dt {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0.4rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--q-muted);
  }

  .privacy {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem 3.5rem;
    margin-top: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    border: 1px solid var(--q-line);
    border-radius: var(--q-radius-lg);
    background: var(--q-panel);
  }

  @media (min-width: 60rem) {
    .privacy {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 2.2fr);
      align-items: start;
    }

    .privacy a {
      grid-column: 2;
    }
  }

  .privacy h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.375rem, 2.4vw, 1.75rem);
  }

  .privacy ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--q-muted);
  }

  .privacy code {
    font-size: 0.875em;
    color: var(--q-text);
  }

  .privacy a {
    justify-self: start;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    color: var(--q-accent);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }
</style>
